# Code Guidelines

1. Verify information before presenting it. Do not assume or speculate without clear evidence.
2. Make changes file by file and give the user a chance to spot mistakes.
3. Preserve existing code; do not remove unrelated code or functionalities.
4. Use explicit, descriptive variable names over short, ambiguous ones.
5. Follow consistent coding style with the project.
6. Prioritize performance where applicable.
7. Consider security implications when modifying code.
8. Suggest or include appropriate unit tests for new or modified code.
9. Implement robust error handling and logging.
10. Encourage modular design for maintainability and reusability.
11. Avoid magic numbers; use named constants.
12. Consider edge cases when implementing logic.
